Here's a basic outline for designing an end-user API for 3D camera animation in TypeScript:

1. Define the API endpoint:
```typescript
export interface AnimateCamera {
  url: string;
  method: 'POST';
  headers: {
    'Content-Type': 'application/json',
  };
  body: {
    // Camera animation parameters
  };
}
```
2. Create a function to make the API call:
```typescript
async function animateCamera(cameraAnimationParams: any): Promise<void> {
  const apiEndpoint: AnimateCamera = {
    url: 'https://example.com/api/animate_camera',
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json',
    },
    body: cameraAnimationParams,
  };

  try {
    await fetch(apiEndpoint.url, {
      method: apiEndpoint.method,
      headers: apiEndpoint.headers,
      body: JSON.stringify(apiEndpoint.body),
    });
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error animating camera:', error);
  }
}
```
3. Use the `animateCamera` function in your application:
```typescript
const cameraAnimationParams = {
  // Your camera animation parameters
};

animateCamera(cameraAnimationParams)
  .then(() => console.log('Camera animated successfully'))
  .catch((error) => console.error('Error animating camera:', error));
```
4. Add additional parameters to the `AnimateCamera` interface as needed to support more complex camera animation scenarios.

