Here's a Dart function that takes a list of transaction objects and returns the top three coins with the highest average profit and the top 3 coins with highest average loss:

```dart
import 'package:collection/collection.dart';

List<Transaction> topProfitCoins(List<Transaction> transactions) {
  return transactions
      .groupBy((transaction) => transaction.coinName)
      .map((coinName, transactions) {
        final totalProfit = transactions.fold(0, (a, b) => a + b.profit);
        final averageProfit = totalProfit / transactions.length;
        return Transaction(coinName, averageProfit);
      })
      .toList()
      .reversed
      .take(3)
      .toList();
}

List<Transaction> topLossCoins(List<Transaction> transactions) {
  return transactions
      .groupBy((transaction) => transaction.coinName)
      .map((coinName, transactions) {
        final totalLoss = transactions.fold(0, (a, b) => a + b.profit * -1);
        final averageLoss = totalLoss / transactions.length;
        return Transaction(coinName, averageLoss);
      })
      .toList()
      .reversed
      .take(3)
      .toList();
}

class Transaction {
  final String coinName;
  final double profit;

  Transaction(this.coinName, this.profit);
}
```

