To use a Gaussian filter before applying the Sobel operator to reduce noise in the image, you can add a few lines of code to your existing MATLAB script. Here's the modified code:

```matlab
% Read input image
input_image = imread('image.jpg');

% Convert to grayscale
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);

% Apply Gaussian filter
gaussian_filtered_image = imfilter(gray_image, fspecial('average', [3 3]));

% Define Sobel operator in x direction
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];

% Define Sobel operator in y direction
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];

% Apply Sobel operator in x direction
edge_image_x = conv2(double(gaussian_filtered_image), sobel_x, 'same');

% Apply Sobel operator in y direction
edge_image_y = conv2(double(gaussian_filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');

% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);

% Display edge image
imshow(edge_image);
```

In this modified code, we first apply a Gaussian filter to the grayscale image using the `imfilter` function and the `fspecial` function to create a 3x3 average filter. This helps to reduce noise in the image before applying the Sobel operator.

To create a NestJS model that creates a MongoDB document with multiple schemas, you can follow these steps:

1. Define your Mongoose schema for each schema.
