1. Next, add the following PHP code to your script to calculate the current time and set the CSS class for the sun image accordingly:
```php
<?php
    $currentTime = time();
    $hour = date('H', $currentTime);

    if ($hour >= 6 && $hour <= 19) {
        echo '<style>.sun { background-image: url("day_sun.png"); }</style>';
    } else {
        echo '<style>.sun { background-image: url("night_sun.png"); }</style>';
    }
?>
```
In this example, we have two images for the sun: `day_sun.png` and `night_sun.png`. The PHP code calculates the current hour and sets the CSS class for the sun image accordingly. During the day (6 AM to 7 PM), the `day_sun.png` image will be used, while during the night (7 PM to 6 AM), the `night_sun.png` image will be used.

1. Finally, add the following CSS code to your stylesheet to define the different styles for the sun image:
```css
.sun {
    width: 100px;
    height: 100px;
}

